scenario ny_n352610 is, as stated in ruling NY N352610:
    % both garments are style 60025T, classified separately
    the knit Henley top is an upper body garment,
        confer "consists of a women’s Henley knit top and a woven bottom".
    the knit Henley top is classified under the US tariff,
        confer "HTSUS, which provides for Women’s or girls’ blouses and shirts".
    the cut of the knit Henley top indicates women,
        confer "consists of a women’s Henley knit top and a woven bottom".
    the fabric construction of the knit Henley top is knitted,
        confer "The upper body garment is constructed from 48% cotton, 48% modal, 4% spandex knit fabric".
    the knit Henley top contains 48 percent of cotton,
        confer "The upper body garment is constructed from 48% cotton, 48% modal, 4% spandex knit fabric".
    the knit Henley top contains 48 percent of modal,
        confer "The upper body garment is constructed from 48% cotton, 48% modal, 4% spandex knit fabric".
    the knit Henley top contains 4 percent of spandex,
        confer "The upper body garment is constructed from 48% cotton, 48% modal, 4% spandex knit fabric".
    the knit Henley top is loose-fitting,
        confer "The loose-fitting garment extends from the shoulders to below the waist and features a Henley neckline".
    the knit Henley top has an opening starting at the neckline,
        confer "a right-over-left, partial front opening with a three-button closure on the placket".
    the knit Henley top closes right over left,
        confer "a right-over-left, partial front opening with a three-button closure on the placket".
    the knit Henley top is claimed to belong to nightwear,
        confer "You state that the garments are intended to be worn as sleepwear".
    the claim that the knit Henley top belongs to nightwear is rejected,
